but first we begin with what's next  after the killing of ayman al-zwahiri  the leader of al-qaeda azwahiri a key  figure in planning the 9 11 attacks died  in a u.s drone strike in afghanistan on  saturday he'd been running al-qaeda  since osama bin laden was killed and led  the terror organization spread to other  countries president biden announced the  news from the white house last night he  said he hopes this would help bring some  closure senior investigative  correspondent katherine herridge is at  the pentagon with more on how exactly  the u.s finally tracked down al-swahiri  katherine good morning  good morning jerica up until a few  months ago the al-qaeda leader's  location was a huge mystery for u.s  intelligence even with a 25 million  dollar bounty on his head now with this  drone strike senior al qaeda leaders  behind 9 11 are either dead or captured  justice has been delivered and this  terrorist leader is no more president  biden approved the precision strike that  killed al qaeda leader ayman al-zawahiri  two hellfire missiles from a u.s drone  killed azrahiri on the balcony of his  hideout in downtown kabul in afghanistan  the mission was a success  none of his family members were hurt and  there were no civilian casualties the  terrorist leader was tracked down  earlier this year in the busy afghan  capital of kabul where he moved to  reunite with family i gave the final  approval to go get him mr biden said the  successful operation could help close a  final chapter of the 9 11 attacks which  killed nearly 3 000 americans 21 years  ago next month al-swahiri was pivotal to  planning the attack it's my hope that  this decisive action will bring one more  measure of closure al-zwahiri also  played a role in al-qaeda attacks that  murdered americans overseas at two u.s  embassies in east africa and on the uss  coal in yemen after navy seals raided  this compound in pakistan 11 years ago  killing al-qaeda founder osama bin laden  as wahiri took over and for years rumors  about his death swirled his location  unknown  after last year's chaotic withdrawal of  u.s forces from afghanistan mr biden  insisted the weekend strike shows the  u.s ability to target terrorists remains  strong no matter how long it takes  no matter where you hide  if you are a threat to our people the  united states will find you and take you  out  a former senior u.s military official  who ran counter-terrorism operations  told cbs news the question now is how  the al qaeda leader could be living in  the afghan capital without the support  of the taliban indicating the  relationship between al qaeda and the  taliban is as strong as ever nate  catherine thank you
 

